      "id": "Excalibur - Recon-T1595-Active Scanning",
      "name": "Excalibur - Recon-T1595-Active Scanning",
      "description": "Simulates active port scanning from a foothold machine (nmap-style TCP connect scan using .NET TcpClient): scans 20 common ports on the configured target (SSH/22, FTP/21, Telnet/23, SMTP/25, HTTP/80, HTTPS/443, SMB/445, RDP/3389, WinRM/5985/5986, MSSQL/1433, MySQL/3306, PostgreSQL/5432, RabbitMQ/5672, Redis/6379, Elasticsearch/9200, Kubernetes/6443, VNC/5900, LDAP/389, LDAPS/636). Also performs an ICMP reachability check and a UDP DNS probe. The combination of rapid sequential TCP connections to multiple well-known service ports from a non-network-tool process is a high-fidelity MDE active scanning behavioral signal. Used by adversaries after initial access to map the internal network from the foothold.",
      "tactic": "Reconnaissance",
      "tcode": "T1595",
      "technique_name": "Active Scanning",
      "executor": "powershell",
