      "id": "Excalibur - Recon-T1590-Gather Victim Network Information",
      "name": "Excalibur - Recon-T1590-Gather Victim Network Information",
      "description": "Performs DNS deep enumeration against a configured target domain from the foothold, simulating adversary network infrastructure mapping: enumerates A, AAAA, MX, NS, TXT (SPF/DKIM/DMARC), SOA, and CNAME records; attempts a DNS zone transfer (AXFR) — adversaries always try this even if it fails; performs subdomain brute-force using a common 20-entry wordlist; does a reverse DNS lookup on the domain's A record IPs; and checks for DNSSEC configuration. High-volume DNS queries with diverse record types from a non-DNS-tool process are MDE DNS reconnaissance behavioral signals.",
