      "name": "Excalibur - Recon-T1592-Gather Victim Host Information (WinPEAS)",
      "description": "WinPEAS-style comprehensive local host enumeration: OS version, build, hotfixes/patches, system uptime, architecture, domain membership, installed software (registry uninstall keys), running services with binary paths, scheduled tasks with actions, local shares, open TCP/UDP ports (netstat-style), startup entries (Run/RunOnce registry), AutoRun locations (HKLM+HKCU Run keys), world-writable directories in system paths, unquoted service path enumeration, weak permission services, clear-text credential file locations (web.config, .env, *.config with 'password', SAM/NTDS/SYSTEM hive presence check). This is the most comprehensive single recon script in the pack — output mirrors a WinPEAS run and generates extensive process and file access telemetry in MDE.",
